'\" t
.nh
.TH podman-container-inspect 1
.SH "نام (NAME)"
podman-container-inspect \- Display a container's configuration

.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBpodman container inspect\fP [\fIoptions\fP] \fIcontainer\fP [\fIcontainer\fP ...]

.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
This displays the low-level information on containers identified by name or ID. By default, this renders
all results in a JSON array. If a format is specified, the given template is executed for each result.

.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.SS \fB--format\fP, \fB-f\fP=\fIformat\fP
Format the output using the given Go template.
The keys of the returned JSON can be used as the values for the --format flag (see examples below).

.PP
Valid placeholders for the Go template are listed below:

.TS
allbox;
l l 
l l .
\fB\fBPlaceholder\fP\fP	\fB\fBDescription\fP\fP
\&.AppArmorProfile	AppArmor profile (string)
\&.Args	T{
Command-line arguments (array of strings)
T}
\&.BoundingCaps	T{
Bounding capability set (array of strings)
T}
\&.Config ...	Structure with config info
\&.ConmonPidFile	T{
Path to file containing conmon pid (string)
T}
\&.Created ...	T{
Container creation time (string, ISO3601)
T}
\&.Dependencies	T{
Dependencies (array of strings)
T}
\&.Driver	Storage driver (string)
\&.EffectiveCaps	T{
Effective capability set (array of strings)
T}
\&.ExecIDs	Exec IDs (array of strings)
\&.GraphDriver ...	T{
Further details of graph driver (struct)
T}
\&.HostConfig ...	Host config details (struct)
\&.HostnamePath	T{
Path to file containing hostname (string)
T}
\&.HostsPath	T{
Path to container /etc/hosts file (string)
T}
\&.ID	T{
Container ID (full 64-char hash)
T}
\&.Image	T{
Container image ID (64-char hash)
T}
\&.ImageDigest	T{
Container image digest (sha256:+64-char hash)
T}
\&.ImageName	Container image name (string)
\&.IsInfra	T{
Is this an infra container? (string: true/false)
T}
\&.IsService	T{
Is this a service container? (string: true/false)
T}
\&.KubeExitCodePropagation	T{
Kube exit-code propagation (string)
T}
\&.LockNumber	T{
Number of the container's Libpod lock
T}
\&.MountLabel	T{
SELinux label of mount (string)
T}
\&.Mounts	Mounts (array of strings)
\&.Name	Container name (string)
\&.Namespace	Container namespace (string)
\&.NetworkSettings ...	Network settings (struct)
\&.OCIConfigPath	T{
Path to OCI config file (string)
T}
\&.OCIRuntime	OCI runtime name (string)
\&.Path	T{
Path to container command (string)
T}
\&.PidFile	T{
Path to file containing container PID (string)
T}
\&.Pod	Parent pod (string)
\&.ProcessLabel	T{
SELinux label of process (string)
T}
\&.ResolvConfPath	T{
Path to container's resolv.conf file (string)
T}
\&.RestartCount	T{
Number of times container has been restarted (int)
T}
\&.Rootfs	Container rootfs (string)
\&.SizeRootFs	Size of rootfs, in bytes [1]
\&.SizeRw	T{
Size of upper (R/W) container layer, in bytes [1]
T}
\&.State ...	Container state info (struct)
\&.StaticDir	T{
Path to container metadata dir (string)
T}
\&.UseImageHostname	T{
Use /etc/hostname from the image if it exists? (string: true/false)
T}
	
\&.UseImageHosts	T{
Use /etc/hosts from the image? (string: true/false)
T}
	
.TE

.PP
[1] This format specifier requires the \fB--size\fP option

.SS \fB--latest\fP, \fB-l\fP
Instead of providing the container name or ID, use the last created container.
Note: the last started container can be from other users of Podman on the host machine.
(This option is not available with the remote Podman client, including Mac and Windows
(excluding WSL2) machines)

.SS \fB--size\fP, \fB-s\fP
In addition to normal output, display the total file size if the type is a container.

.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
Inspect the specified container and print its information in json format.

.EX
